        "original_id": "3c250206-ae47-5ad7-b8a3-338198785e93",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kevin Richardson, AJ McLean, Morgan Taylor Reid, Mika Guillory, Brian Littrell\n- Music Groups: Backstreet Boys\n- Songs: \"Show 'Em (What You're Made Of)\"\n- Albums: In a World Like This\n- Organizations: Kentucky Music Hall of Fame\n- Topics: songwriting, music career, hall of fame inductions\n\nFacts:\n- Kevin Scott Richardson was born on October 3, 1971, and he is an American singer, songwriter, actor, and model best known as a member of the Backstreet Boys.\n- \"Show 'Em (What You're Made Of)\" is a song by the American pop group Backstreet Boys from their eighth studio album In a World Like This.\n- \"Show 'Em (What You're Made Of)\" was written by Morgan Taylor Reid, Mika Guillory, Backstreet Boys member AJ McLean, and Backstreet Boys member Kevin Richardson.\n- Kevin Richardson was inducted into the Kentucky Music Hall of Fame with his cousin and Backstreet Boys bandmate Brian Littrell on April 10, 2015.",
